;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; CLASSPAD config.bib, Windows CE 5.0: the image executes in place from the
; NOR flash (XIP). Two regions, as the CE 6.0 image had (docs/03); swapped
; on 2026-11-09 so that the part worth keeping survives Casio's boots:
;   NK   the kernel, the shell, the drivers and the BSP's own programs, in
;        the erased hole inside Casio's OS image (P1 0x80EE0000, 5 MiB), which
;        Casio's OS never writes after an OS update: flashed once by
;        wince.hhk / nkflash.hhk and kept (translator NK_WINDOW=hole, the
;        default). This file. The 2026-11-09 image fills 4.9 MB of it.
;   EXT  a second XIP region in the eActivity area of the chip (P1
;        0x83860000, 7.625 MiB): Math Xpander and the libraries only it needs
;        (platform.bib entries with EXT in the region column). Casio's OS
;        reformats the area at every boot that finds it holding something
;        else, so wince.hhk reflashes EXT.bin before a CE session when it
;        differs, or skips it on request. OEMInit hands the region to the
;        kernel through OEMRomChain (SRC\INC\classpad_extrom.h); without it
;        CE boots as if the region were empty.
;
; CE 5.0's romimage (4.0) cannot lay out two regions that are not
; contiguous: given both MEMORY lines it placed NK at EXT's address and EXT
; right after NK's end, whatever the addresses said (2026-11-09 makeimg.log:
; "RAM AutoSize: RAM Start=813c1000", nk.exe at 80ee0000, Math Xpander at
; 81443000..818eb000, then an assertion while finishing NK.bin). CE 6.0's
; romimage honoured them. So the CE 5.0 build makes EXT in a second romimage
; run: PostFmergeBib.bat moves the EXT entries out of ce.bib into
; ext.modules.bib / ext.files.bib, romimage builds NK alone from this file,
; and PostRomImage.bat assembles ext.bib from ext.bib.hdr (the EXT region's
; own MEMORY and CONFIG) and those entries and runs romimage again. The DLL
; address ranges of the two runs must not overlap (every ROM DLL has a fixed
; virtual address): NK's SH4 DLLs put their data pages top-down from
; 0x02000000 (a few KiB each, 33 DLLs: 1 MiB is plenty) and their code in
; slot 1 top-down from 0x04000000 (4.1 MiB); EXT's Pocket PC modules have no
; .rel files ("old fixup style") and go whole into the data range, 5.1 MiB
; for 25 modules, plus 128 KiB of code range. Hence:
;   NK   data 01F00000..02000000   code 02400000..04000000  (here)
;   EXT  data 01400000..01F00000   code 02100000..02400000  (ext.bib.hdr)
; (EXT's code range was 1 MiB until WordPad and the card games moved there,
; 2026-11-09: their SH4 DLLs, riched20 first, need about 1 MiB of it in 64 KiB
; steps; NK uses 4.1 MiB of its 28.)
; Processes keep slot 0 below 0x01400000 (20 MiB; the default boundary is
; 0x01800000). No AUTOSIZE: in this romimage DLLADDR_AUTOSIZE only works
; under AUTOSIZE=ON, which also moves RAM behind the image.
;
; The whole guest RAM window 0x8C000000-0x8C7FFFFF is RAM (dbt/Makefile owns
; these numbers); the first page is the BOOTARGS page, the last page the
; debug ring shared with the translator (image_cfg.h), both kept out of RAM.
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MEMORY
;   Name        Start     Size      Type
;   -------     --------  --------  ----
    BOOTARGS    8C000000  00001000  RESERVED    ; OAL argument page (unused for now)
    NK          80EE0000  00500000  RAMIMAGE    ; the hole in Casio's OS image, 5 MiB (RAMIMAGE is the only image type; XIP follows from the address)
;   NK          83860000  007A0000  RAMIMAGE    ; the layout until 2026-11-09: NK in the eActivity area (make NK_WINDOW=eact), EXT in the hole
;   EXT         83860000  007A0000  RAMIMAGE    ; the eActivity area, 7.625 MiB: built by the second romimage run, ext.bib.hdr
    RAM         8C001000  007FE000  RAM         ; up to 0x8C7FF000 (dbt/Makefile GUEST_RAM_HI - 4 KiB)
    DBGRING     8C7FF000  00001000  RESERVED    ; translator debug ring (image_cfg.h CLASSPAD_DBG_RING_PA)

CONFIG
    KERNELFIXUPS=ON
    AUTOSIZE=OFF
    DLLLOWADDR      NK   01F00000
    DLLHIGHADDR     NK   02000000
    DLLLOWCODEADDR  NK   02400000
    DLLHIGHCODEADDR NK   04000000
    ROMSTART=80EE0000
    ROMSIZE=00500000
    ROMWIDTH=32
; No profiler symbol tables (romimage writes one per module when PROFILE is
; on; the CE 5.0 makeimg of 2026-11-09 died while printing them)
    PROFILE=OFF
; No compression: the writable sections are stored as is, so the kernel
; does not run its decompressor at boot (slow under the translator) and
; the image is a few hundred KB larger.
    COMPRESSION=OFF
; ROMFLAGS: bit 0 would disable demand paging, bit 1 the full kernel mode
; (CE 5.0 drivers and GWES run in kernel mode, which the MMIO macros of the
; drivers need), bit 4 "trust only ROM modules". Keep all off.
    ROMFLAGS=00
; RAM file system (object store) share of RAM, per 2 MiB band: 8 of 256
; (3.1 %, about 256 KiB of the 8 MiB window) instead of the default 50 %.
; The kernel carves these pages out at boot and never lends them back; the
; object store is the root file system and holds the registry, so it stays
; non-zero. The default left so few pages with 9 MiB of RAM that the kernel
; refused the display driver's data copy and GWES started without a driver
; (CE 6.0, 2026-11-03).
    FSRAMPERCENT=08080808
